=begin
  calendar_sagapanel.lic

  Saga-only panel for the GemStone IV live events calendar shown on
  play.net/gs4, plus the TownCrier GS Calendar (gstowncrier.com). Reads seven
  public Google calendars (Prime, Premium, Platinum, General, Cooperative
  Houses, Meeting Hall Organizations, TownCrier), expands recurring events,
  and shows them in your local time. Toggle between Upcoming, Week and Month
  views; click a day or an event for details. Click the + beside an event to
  set an alarm that echoes warnings before it starts; about a minute after
  login, every alarm you have set is listed once, soonest first.

  Each calendar can be switched on or off; the defaults follow your game
  instance (Prime/Premium or Platinum). Feeds are cached in data/calendar_cache
  and re-downloaded every 6 hours or on *cal refresh.

  Commands:
    *cal                        - Show the Upcoming view.
    *cal alarm <n>              - Set/clear an alarm on an event (the + / alarm clock does this).
    *cal alarms                 - List alarms that are set.
    *cal alarmtest              - Echo a sample alarm for a random upcoming event (nothing is saved).
    *cal back                   - Return from an event or day to the previous view.
    *cal combine                - Mix all calendars into one list (the default).
    *cal day <YYYY-MM-DD>       - Show one day's events.
    *cal event <n>              - Show an event's details.
    *cal goto <room>            - Copy a room number to the clipboard and go2 there.
    *cal group                  - Separate the lists into one section per calendar.
    *cal help                   - List commands.
    *cal month                  - Show the Month view.
    *cal next / *cal prev       - Move forward/back a week, month or day.
    *cal refresh                - Re-download all calendars now.
    *cal show <calendar>        - Toggle a calendar (prime, premium, platinum, general, houses, mho, towncrier).
    *cal today                  - Jump back to the current week/month/day.
    *cal up <calendar>          - Move a calendar up in the grouped list (the up arrow).
    *cal upcoming               - Show the Upcoming view.
    *cal week                   - Show the Week view.

  Author: Claude Code(Creator and Feature Additions), Codex(Bug Fixes and Review), RuseofFools (Very Little)
  Required: Lich >= 5.20.0
  Tags: saga, frontend, mod, window, panel, calendar, events, schedule
  Version: 1.8.0

  Recently changed:
    v1.8.0  (2026-11-13)
      - Added *cal alarmtest; *calendar works as well as *cal; fixed alarms failing to save on some Lich versions.
    v1.7.0  (2026-11-13)
      - Up arrows reorder grouped calendars; room numbers in event details copy and go2.
    v1.6.0  (2026-11-13)
      - Added *cal group / *cal combine to list events by calendar or all together (default).
    v1.5.0  (2026-11-13)
      - Calendars download in parallel in the background; fixed cut-off descriptions from the cache.
    v1.4.0  (2026-11-13)
      - Lists all alarmed events, soonest first, once about a minute after login.
    v1.3.0  (2026-11-13)
      - Click + beside an event to set an alarm; echoes warnings at 60/45/30/15/5 minutes.
    v1.2.0  (2026-11-13)
      - Every entry shows one [key] for its calendar ([TC] for TownCrier); existing keys merged, never doubled.
    v1.1.0  (2026-11-13)
      - Added the TownCrier GS Calendar (gstowncrier.com) as a seventh calendar, on by default.
    v1.0.0  (2026-11-13)
      - Initial release.
=end

require 'net/http'
require 'uri'
require 'date'
require 'time'
require 'cgi'
require 'fileutils'
require 'tzinfo'

no_kill_all

# --- BEGIN CALENDAR ENGINE --- (pure Ruby, no Lich calls)
module CalendarEngine
  Event = Struct.new(:uid, :cal, :summary, :description, :location, :start, :finish, :all_day,
                     :tzid, :rrule, :exdates, :recurrence_id, :cancelled)
  Occurrence = Struct.new(:event, :start, :finish, :all_day)

  WEEKDAYS = { 'SU' => 0, 'MO' => 1, 'TU' => 2, 'WE' => 3, 'TH' => 4, 'FR' => 5, 'SA' => 6 }.freeze
  MAX_STEPS = 6000

  # ---------- ICS parsing ----------

  # Any run of CRs before a newline counts as one line break, and stray CRs are
  # dropped: a cache saved by an older version in Windows text mode has
  # "\r\r\n" endings, which left a CR mid-description that cut the text off.
  def self.unfold(text)
    text.gsub(/\r*\n/, "\n").delete("\r").gsub(/\n[ \t]/, '').split("\n")
  end

  def self.unescape(value)
    value.gsub(/\\([nN,;\\])/) do
      ch = Regexp.last_match(1)
      ch.casecmp?('n') ? "\n" : ch
    end
  end

  # Returns [kind, value]: [:date, Date], [:utc, Time] or [:local, [y, m, d, h, mi, s], tzid]
  def self.parse_time(params, value)
    value = value.strip
    if params['VALUE'] == 'DATE' || value =~ /\A\d{8}\z/
      [:date, Date.strptime(value[0, 8], '%Y%m%d')]
    elsif value.end_with?('Z')
      [:utc, Time.utc(*value.scan(/\A(\d{4})(\d\d)(\d\d)T(\d\d)(\d\d)(\d\d)/).first.map(&:to_i))]
    else
      parts = value.scan(/\A(\d{4})(\d\d)(\d\d)T(\d\d)(\d\d)(\d\d)/).first.map(&:to_i)
      [:local, parts, params['TZID']]
    end
  end

  def self.zone(tzid)
    @zones ||= {}
    @zones[tzid] ||= (TZInfo::Timezone.get(tzid) rescue nil)
  end

  # Wall-clock time in a zone -> UTC Time.
  def self.local_to_utc(parts, tzid)
    tz = tzid && zone(tzid)
    naive = Time.utc(*parts)
    return naive unless tz

    tz.local_to_utc(naive, true) rescue tz.local_to_utc(naive)
  rescue StandardError
    naive
  end

  def self.to_time(parsed)
    case parsed[0]
    when :date  then Time.local(parsed[1].year, parsed[1].month, parsed[1].day)
    when :utc   then parsed[1]
    else local_to_utc(parsed[1], parsed[2])
    end
  end

  def self.parse_ics(text, cal)
    events = []
    cur = nil
    unfold(text.dup.force_encoding('UTF-8').scrub('?')).each do |line|
      if line == 'BEGIN:VEVENT'
        cur = { exdates: [] }
        next
      elsif line == 'END:VEVENT'
        ev = build_event(cur, cal)
        events << ev if ev
        cur = nil
        next
      end
      next unless cur && line =~ /\A([A-Z-]+)((?:;[^:]*)?):(.*)\z/

      name = Regexp.last_match(1)
      params = Regexp.last_match(2).split(';').reject(&:empty?).map { |p| p.split('=', 2) }.to_h
      value = Regexp.last_match(3)
      case name
      when 'UID', 'SUMMARY', 'DESCRIPTION', 'LOCATION', 'STATUS', 'RRULE' then cur[name] = value
      when 'DTSTART', 'DTEND', 'RECURRENCE-ID' then cur[name] = parse_time(params, value)
      when 'EXDATE' then value.split(',').each { |v| cur[:exdates] << parse_time(params, v) }
      end
    end
    events
  end

  def self.build_event(h, cal)
    return nil unless h['DTSTART']

    start = h['DTSTART']
    all_day = start[0] == :date
    finish = h['DTEND']
    s = to_time(start)
    f = finish ? to_time(finish) : (all_day ? s + 86_400 : s)
    Event.new(h['UID'], cal, unescape(h['SUMMARY'].to_s), unescape(h['DESCRIPTION'].to_s),
              unescape(h['LOCATION'].to_s), start, f - s, all_day,
              start[0] == :local ? start[2] : nil, h['RRULE'],
              h[:exdates].map { |x| to_time(x) },
              h['RECURRENCE-ID'] ? to_time(h['RECURRENCE-ID']) : nil,
              h['STATUS'] == 'CANCELLED')
  end

  # ---------- recurrence ----------

  def self.parse_rrule(str)
    str.split(';').map { |p| p.split('=', 2) }.to_h
  end

  # The event's start as wall-clock [Date, h, mi, s] in its own zone, so
  # recurrences keep their local time across daylight-saving changes.
  def self.wall_start(ev)
    case ev.start[0]
    when :date  then [ev.start[1], 0, 0, 0]
    when :utc   then t = ev.start[1]; [Date.new(t.year, t.month, t.day), t.hour, t.min, t.sec]
    else p = ev.start[1]; [Date.new(p[0], p[1], p[2]), p[3], p[4], p[5]]
    end
  end

  def self.occurrence_time(ev, date, h, mi, s)
    case ev.start[0]
    when :date  then Time.local(date.year, date.month, date.day)
    when :utc   then Time.utc(date.year, date.month, date.day, h, mi, s)
    else local_to_utc([date.year, date.month, date.day, h, mi, s], ev.tzid)
    end
  end

  # nth weekday of a month: nth 1..5 or -1..-5; nil if it doesn't exist.
  def self.nth_weekday(year, month, wday, nth)
    if nth > 0
      first = Date.new(year, month, 1)
      d = first + ((wday - first.wday) % 7) + 7 * (nth - 1)
      d.month == month ? d : nil
    else
      last = Date.new(year, month, -1)
      d = last - ((last.wday - wday) % 7) - 7 * (-nth - 1)
      d.month == month ? d : nil
    end
  end

  def self.byday_dates(year, month, byday, fallback_day)
    return [Date.new(year, month, fallback_day)] if byday.nil? && Date.valid_date?(year, month, fallback_day)
    return [] if byday.nil?

    byday.split(',').flat_map do |token|
      m = token.match(/\A([+-]?\d+)?([A-Z]{2})\z/)
      next [] unless m && WEEKDAYS[m[2]]

      wday = WEEKDAYS[m[2]]
      if m[1]
        [nth_weekday(year, month, wday, m[1].to_i)].compact
      else
        (1..Date.new(year, month, -1).day).map { |d| Date.new(year, month, d) }.select { |d| d.wday == wday }
      end
    end.sort
  end

  # Yields each candidate date of the rule, in order, starting at the event's first date.
  def self.each_rule_date(rule, first)
    interval = [rule['INTERVAL'].to_i, 1].max
    case rule['FREQ']
    when 'DAILY'
      MAX_STEPS.times { |k| yield first + k * interval }
    when 'WEEKLY'
      wkst = WEEKDAYS[rule['WKST'] || 'MO']
      days = (rule['BYDAY'] || %w[SU MO TU WE TH FR SA][first.wday]).split(',').map { |d| WEEKDAYS[d[-2, 2]] }.compact
      week0 = first - ((first.wday - wkst) % 7)
      MAX_STEPS.times do |k|
        ws = week0 + 7 * interval * k
        days.map { |wd| ws + ((wd - wkst) % 7) }.sort.each { |d| yield d if d >= first }
      end
    when 'MONTHLY'
      MAX_STEPS.times do |k|
        m = first >> (interval * k)
        dates = if rule['BYMONTHDAY']
                  rule['BYMONTHDAY'].split(',').map(&:to_i).filter_map do |md|
                    md = Date.new(m.year, m.month, -1).day + md + 1 if md.negative?
                    Date.valid_date?(m.year, m.month, md) ? Date.new(m.year, m.month, md) : nil
                  end
                else
                  byday_dates(m.year, m.month, rule['BYDAY'], first.day)
                end
        dates.sort.each { |d| yield d if d >= first }
      end
    when 'YEARLY'
      months = rule['BYMONTH'] ? rule['BYMONTH'].split(',').map(&:to_i) : [first.month]
      (MAX_STEPS / 12).times do |k|
        year = first.year + interval * k
        months.sort.each do |mo|
          byday_dates(year, mo, rule['BYDAY'], first.day).each { |d| yield d if d >= first }
        end
      end
    end
  end

  def self.expand(ev, from, to, overridden)
    return [] if ev.cancelled

    duration = ev.finish
    unless ev.rrule
      s = to_time(ev.start)
      return s < to && s + duration > from ? [Occurrence.new(ev, s, s + duration, ev.all_day)] : []
    end

    rule = parse_rrule(ev.rrule)
    until_t = rule['UNTIL'] ? to_time(parse_time({}, rule['UNTIL'])) : nil
    count = rule['COUNT'] ? rule['COUNT'].to_i : nil
    exset = ev.exdates.map(&:to_i)
    first, h, mi, sec = wall_start(ev)
    out = []
    n = 0
    each_rule_date(rule, first) do |date|
      t = occurrence_time(ev, date, h, mi, sec)
      break if until_t && t > until_t
      break if count && n >= count
      break if t >= to

      n += 1
      next if exset.include?(t.to_i)
      next if overridden.include?([ev.uid, t.to_i])

      out << Occurrence.new(ev, t, t + duration, ev.all_day) if t + duration > from
    end
    out
  end

  # All occurrences overlapping [from, to), sorted by start.
  def self.occurrences(events, from, to)
    overridden = {}
    events.each { |e| overridden[[e.uid, e.recurrence_id.to_i]] = true if e.recurrence_id }
    events.flat_map { |e| expand(e, from, to, e.recurrence_id ? {} : overridden) }
          .sort_by { |o| [o.start, o.all_day ? 0 : 1, o.event.summary] }
  end

  # ---------- text ----------

  # Codepoints, not literals, so this file stays pure ASCII (repository.lic
  # rejects non-ASCII source).
  ASCII_MAP = {
    0x2018 => "'", 0x2019 => "'", 0x201C => '"', 0x201D => '"', 0x2013 => '-', 0x2014 => '--',
    0x2026 => '...', 0x00A0 => ' ', 0x2022 => '*', 0x00D7 => 'x', 0x200B => '', 0xFEFF => ''
  }.freeze

  def self.to_ascii(text)
    text.to_s.dup.force_encoding('UTF-8').scrub('?').gsub(/[^\x00-\x7F]/) do |c|
      ASCII_MAP[c.ord] || begin
        plain = c.unicode_normalize(:nfkd).gsub(/[^\x00-\x7F]/, '')
        plain.empty? ? '?' : plain
      end
    end
  end

  # Google Calendar descriptions are HTML fragments.
  def self.plain_text(html)
    text = html.gsub(%r{<br\s*/?>}i, "\n").gsub(%r{</(p|div|li)>}i, "\n").gsub(/<li[^>]*>/i, '- ')
               .gsub(/<a [^>]*href="([^"]*)"[^>]*>(.*?)<\/a>/im) do
                 href = Regexp.last_match(1)
                 label = Regexp.last_match(2).gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '').strip
                 label.empty? || label == href || href.include?(label) ? href : "#{label} (#{href})"
               end
               .gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '')
    CGI.unescapeHTML(text).gsub(/[ \t]+\n/, "\n").gsub(/\n{3,}/, "\n\n").strip
  end
end
# --- END CALENDAR ENGINE ---

module CalendarPanel
  WINDOW_ID = 'calendar_sagapanel'.freeze
  # tag: the [key] shown in front of every entry from that calendar.
  # same: matches an existing leading [key] that already names this calendar
  # (including the typos and variants found in the feeds), so it isn't doubled.
  CALENDARS = [
    { key: 'prime',     name: 'Prime',     id: 'pcab6kb6qe76j3fl2afq9q699s', tag: 'Prime',    same: /\bprime\b/i },
    { key: 'premium',   name: 'Premium',   id: 'j6q1n0lq7vf222o6kltaupa01s', tag: 'Premium',  same: /\bpremi/i },
    { key: 'platinum',  name: 'Platinum',  id: 'jv19jhbr7fepl3rfh474l5udgc', tag: 'Platinum', same: /\b(plat|patinum)/i },
    { key: 'general',   name: 'General',   id: 't1vglkquofrk91qkbo8stl756g', tag: 'General',  same: /\Ageneral\z/i },
    { key: 'houses',    name: 'Houses',    id: 'n058u7qetmcm2p49p7s650v5e0', tag: 'CHEs',     same: /\bches?\b/i },
    { key: 'mho',       name: 'MHO',       id: 'j92j2chtbqu5bob9scv0u2hlfo', tag: 'MHOs',     same: /\bmhos?\b/i },
    { key: 'towncrier', name: 'TownCrier', id: 'eg1304nmvgiad028n96rnqqb2c', tag: 'TC',       same: /\A(tc|towncrier)\z/i }
  ].freeze
  FEED_URL = 'https://calendar.google.com/calendar/ical/%s%%40group.calendar.google.com/public/basic.ics'.freeze
  USER_AGENT = 'Lich5-calendar-panel/1.0'.freeze
  REFRESH_SECONDS = 6 * 60 * 60
  UPCOMING_DAYS = 7
  UPCOMING_MAX = 40
  MONTH_CELL = 8 # widest cell is "[30](12)"

  @queue = Queue.new
  @events = {}       # cal key => [Event]
  @loaded_at = nil
  @downloading = false
  @arrived = 0
  @view = :upcoming  # :upcoming, :week, :month, :day, :event
  @anchor = Date.today
  @stack = []       # previous [view, anchor, detail] for *cal back
  @shown = []        # occurrences linked from the current screen, by index
  @detail = nil

  class << self
    attr_reader :queue
  end

  # ---------- settings ----------

  def self.default_enabled
    if XMLData.game.to_s =~ /plat/i
      %w[platinum general houses mho towncrier]
    else
      %w[prime premium general houses mho towncrier]
    end
  end

  def self.enabled
    list = plain(CharSettings['calendars'])
    list.is_a?(Array) ? list : default_enabled
  end

  def self.toggle_calendar(key)
    cal = CALENDARS.find { |c| c[:key] == key.downcase || c[:name].casecmp?(key) }
    return respond("Calendar: There is no calendar named '#{key}'. The calendars are #{sentence_list(CALENDARS.map { |c| c[:key] })}.") unless cal

    list = enabled.dup
    list.include?(cal[:key]) ? list.delete(cal[:key]) : list << cal[:key]
    CharSettings['calendars'] = list
    render
  end

  # ---------- feeds ----------

  def self.cache_dir
    dir = File.join($data_dir, 'calendar_cache')
    FileUtils.mkdir_p(dir)
    dir
  end

  def self.cache_file(cal)
    File.join(cache_dir, "#{cal[:key]}.ics")
  end

  def self.http_get(url, limit = 4)
    uri = URI(url)
    response = Net::HTTP.start(uri.host, uri.port, use_ssl: true, open_timeout: 10, read_timeout: 30) do |http|
      req = Net::HTTP::Get.new(uri)
      req['User-Agent'] = USER_AGENT
      http.request(req)
    end
    if response.is_a?(Net::HTTPRedirection) && limit > 0
      return http_get(URI.join(url, response['location']).to_s, limit - 1)
    end
    raise "HTTP #{response.code}" unless response.is_a?(Net::HTTPSuccess)

    response.body.to_s.dup.force_encoding('UTF-8')
  end

  KEEP_HISTORY = 400 * 86_400 # one-time events that ended longer ago than this are dropped

  def self.parse(body, cal)
    cutoff = Time.now - KEEP_HISTORY
    CalendarEngine.parse_ics(body, cal[:key]).select do |e|
      e.rrule || CalendarEngine.to_time(e.start) + e.finish > cutoff
    end
  end

  def self.load_cached!
    CALENDARS.each do |cal|
      path = cache_file(cal)
      next unless File.exist?(path)

      @events[cal[:key]] = parse(File.binread(path).force_encoding('UTF-8'), cal)
      @loaded_at = [@loaded_at, File.mtime(path)].compact.min
    end
  end

  def self.stale?
    !@downloading && (@loaded_at.nil? || Time.now - @loaded_at > REFRESH_SECONDS)
  end

  def self.downloading?
    @downloading
  end

  # Downloads every calendar at once on background threads, so the panel stays
  # clickable. Results are handed back through @arrivals and applied by
  # poll_refresh! on the script's own thread.
  def self.start_refresh!(announce: false)
    return respond('Calendar: The calendars are already being updated.') if @downloading && announce
    return if @downloading

    @downloading = true
    @announce = announce
    @errors = []
    @arrived = 0
    @arrivals = Queue.new
    @first_load = @events.empty?
    render if @first_load
    arrivals = @arrivals
    Thread.new do
      workers = CALENDARS.map do |cal|
        Thread.new do
          body = http_get(format(FEED_URL, cal[:id]))
          raise 'not a calendar' unless body.include?('BEGIN:VCALENDAR')

          arrivals << [cal, body, nil] # reported as soon as this one finishes
        rescue StandardError => e
          arrivals << [cal, nil, e.message]
        end
      end
      workers.each(&:join)
      arrivals << :done
    end
  end

  def self.poll_refresh!
    return unless @downloading

    while (item = (@arrivals.pop(true) rescue nil))
      if item == :done
        @downloading = false
        if @errors.size == CALENDARS.size
          @loaded_at = Time.now - REFRESH_SECONDS + 600 # all failed: try again in 10 minutes
        else
          @loaded_at = Time.now
        end
        unless @errors.empty?
          noun = @errors.size == 1 ? 'calendar' : 'calendars'
          respond("Calendar: The #{sentence_list(@errors)} #{noun} could not be updated, so the saved copies are being used.")
        end
        respond('Calendar: All calendars have been updated.') if @announce && @errors.empty?
        render
        return
      end

      cal, body, error = item
      @arrived += 1
      if body
        File.binwrite(cache_file(cal), body) # binary: never rewrite the feed's CRLF line endings
        @events[cal[:key]] = parse(body, cal)
      else
        @errors << "#{cal[:name]} (#{error})"
      end
      render if @first_load # fill the panel in as each calendar arrives on a first run
    end
  end

  # ["a", "b", "c"] -> "a, b and c"
  def self.sentence_list(items)
    items = items.map(&:to_s)
    return items.join if items.size < 2

    "#{items[0..-2].join(', ')} and #{items[-1]}"
  end

  def self.events
    enabled.flat_map { |k| @events[k] || [] }
  end

  # ---------- formatting ----------

  def self.xml(text)
    CalendarEngine.to_ascii(text).gsub('&', '&amp;').gsub('<', '&lt;').gsub('>', '&gt;').gsub("'", '&apos;').gsub('"', '&quot;')
  end

  def self.dlink(cmd, label)
    "<d cmd='#{xml(cmd)}'>#{xml(label)}</d>"
  end

  def self.write(lines)
    _respond("<clearStream id='#{WINDOW_ID}'/>")
    _respond("<pushStream id='#{WINDOW_ID}'/>#{lines.join("\n")}\n<popStream/>\r\n")
  end

  # Windows spells zones out ("Central Standard Time"); shorten to "CST".
  def self.zone_abbr(time)
    name = time.getlocal.strftime('%Z')
    name.size > 5 ? name.scan(/\b[A-Z]/).join : name
  end

  def self.local(time)
    time.getlocal
  end

  def self.time_label(occ)
    return 'All day ' if occ.all_day

    local(occ.start).strftime('%l:%M %p').rjust(8)
  end

  def self.day_bounds(date)
    [Time.local(date.year, date.month, date.day), Time.local((date + 1).year, (date + 1).month, (date + 1).day)]
  end

  # Every entry gets exactly one leading [key] naming its calendar:
  #   "Rogue Guild Night"            -> "[General] Rogue Guild Night"
  #   "[Prime] Crimson Legion"       -> unchanged (already names its calendar)
  #   "[Cysaegir] Moot" (Prime)      -> "[Prime: Cysaegir] Moot"
  #   "[Prime] [EG] Script Swap"     -> "[Prime: EG] Script Swap"
  # All leading keys are merged into one, so there is never a "[ ] [ ]" pair.
  # "[Prime}" (a typo in the feed) counts as a key too.
  def self.title(ev)
    cal = CALENDARS.find { |c| c[:key] == ev.cal }
    rest = ev.summary.strip
    return rest unless cal

    keys = []
    while (m = rest.match(/\A\[([^\]\}]*)[\]\}]\s*/))
      keys << m[1].strip
      rest = m.post_match
    end
    keys = keys.reject(&:empty?).uniq { |k| k.downcase }
    own = keys.find { |k| k =~ cal[:same] }
    others = keys.reject { |k| k =~ cal[:same] }
    key = own || cal[:tag]
    key += ": #{others.join(', ')}" unless others.empty?
    "[#{key}] #{rest}"
  end

  def self.event_line(occ)
    @shown << occ
    n = @shown.size - 1
    "#{alarm_marker(occ, n)} #{time_label(occ)}  #{dlink("*cal event #{n}", title(occ.event))}"
  end

  def self.day_header(date)
    label = date.strftime('%a %b %-d')
    label += ' (today)' if date == Date.today
    dlink("*cal day #{date.iso8601}", label)
  end

  def self.header(nav)
    lines = ['<pushBold/>GemStone IV Calendar<popBold/>']
    views = { upcoming: 'Upcoming', week: 'Week', month: 'Month' }.map do |v, name|
      @view == v ? "[#{name}]" : dlink("*cal #{v}", name)
    end
    lines << views.join('  ')
    if %i[upcoming week day].include?(@view)
      lines << (grouped? ? "#{dlink('*cal combine', 'Combined')}  [By calendar]" : "[Combined]  #{dlink('*cal group', 'By calendar')}")
    end
    lines << "#{dlink('*cal prev', '< prev')}  #{dlink('*cal today', 'today')}  #{dlink('*cal next', 'next >')}" if nav
    lines << CALENDARS.map { |c| dlink("*cal show #{c[:key]}", "#{enabled.include?(c[:key]) ? '[x]' : '[ ]'} #{c[:name]}") }.join(' ')
    updated = if @downloading
                "downloading calendars (#{@arrived}/#{CALENDARS.size})..."
              elsif @loaded_at
                "updated #{((Time.now - @loaded_at) / 60).round} min ago"
              else
                'not loaded yet'
              end
    lines << "Local time (#{zone_abbr(Time.now)}), #{updated}  #{dlink('*cal refresh', '[refresh]')}"
    lines << ''
    lines
  end

  # ---------- section order (grouped view) ----------

  UP_ARROW = '&#x2191;'.freeze # as an entity so this file stays ASCII

  # Calendar keys in the player's chosen order; new calendars go at the end.
  def self.order
    keys = CALENDARS.map { |c| c[:key] }
    saved = plain(CharSettings['order'])
    list = saved.is_a?(Array) ? (saved & keys) : []
    list + (keys - list)
  end

  # Moves a calendar above the section currently shown just before it, so a
  # click always visibly moves it even when hidden or empty calendars sit between.
  def self.move_up(key)
    key = key.to_s.downcase
    cal = CALENDARS.find { |c| c[:key] == key }
    return respond("Calendar: There is no calendar named '#{key}'.") unless cal

    visible = @visible_sections || []
    pos = visible.index(key)
    return respond("Calendar: #{cal[:name]} is already at the top of the list.") if pos.nil? || pos.zero?

    list = order
    list.delete(key)
    list.insert(list.index(visible[pos - 1]), key)
    CharSettings['order'] = list
    render
  end

  # ---------- room links ----------

  # Room numbers as the calendars write them. Bare numbers need 6+ digits (game
  # room UIDs), so years like (2026) and street numbers are never linked.
  # :auto means 6+ digits is a game room UID, fewer is a Lich room ID.
  ROOM_PATTERNS = [
    [/\bLich\s*(?:ID|Room)?\s*[#:]?\s*#?\s*(\d{2,6})\b/i, :lich], # Lich 1234, Lich#1234, Lich ID: 1234, Lich Room #1234
    [/\brn\s*[#:]?\s*(\d{2,8})\b/i,                     :auto], # (rn 1438) -- TownCrier's style
    [/\broom\s*#\s*(\d{2,8})\b/i,                       :auto], # room #1234
    [/\(Room\s*#?\s*(\d{2,8})\)/i,                      :auto], # (Room 1234)
    [/\bu(\d{4,8})\b/,                                  :uid],  # u7132103
    [/\((\d{6,8})\)/,                                   :uid],  # (3209357)
    [/\]\s*(\d{6,8})\b/,                                :uid],  # [Place] 3209357
    [/\s-\s(\d{6,8})\s*\z/,                             :uid]   # Place - 3209357
  ].freeze

  # Wraps each room number in already-escaped panel text with a *cal goto link.
  def self.link_rooms(escaped)
    out = escaped.dup
    ROOM_PATTERNS.each do |pattern, kind|
      out = out.gsub(pattern) do |match|
        num = Regexp.last_match(1)
        next match if match.include?('<d cmd=') # already linked by an earlier pattern

        ref = case kind
              when :lich then num
              when :uid then "u#{num}"
              else num.size >= 6 ? "u#{num}" : num
              end
        match.sub(num, "<d cmd='*cal goto #{ref}'>#{num}</d>")
      end
    end
    out
  end

  # Same approach as exitwindow.lic: write Unicode text straight to the Windows
  # clipboard through user32/kernel32 (no gems needed), then fall back to the
  # platform's clipboard command.
  def self.copy_to_windows_clipboard(text)
    return false unless Gem.win_platform?

    require 'fiddle'
    user32 = Fiddle.dlopen('user32.dll')
    kernel32 = Fiddle.dlopen('kernel32.dll')
    fn = ->(lib, name, args, ret) { Fiddle::Function.new(lib[name], args, ret) }
    open_clipboard  = fn.call(user32, 'OpenClipboard', [Fiddle::TYPE_VOIDP], Fiddle::TYPE_INT)
    close_clipboard = fn.call(user32, 'CloseClipboard', [], Fiddle::TYPE_INT)
    empty_clipboard = fn.call(user32, 'EmptyClipboard', [], Fiddle::TYPE_INT)
    set_data        = fn.call(user32, 'SetClipboardData', [Fiddle::TYPE_UINT, Fiddle::TYPE_VOIDP], Fiddle::TYPE_VOIDP)
    global_alloc    = fn.call(kernel32, 'GlobalAlloc', [Fiddle::TYPE_UINT, Fiddle::TYPE_SIZE_T], Fiddle::TYPE_VOIDP)
    global_free     = fn.call(kernel32, 'GlobalFree', [Fiddle::TYPE_VOIDP], Fiddle::TYPE_VOIDP)
    global_lock     = fn.call(kernel32, 'GlobalLock', [Fiddle::TYPE_VOIDP], Fiddle::TYPE_VOIDP)
    global_unlock   = fn.call(kernel32, 'GlobalUnlock', [Fiddle::TYPE_VOIDP], Fiddle::TYPE_INT)

    opened = false
    5.times do
      break if (opened = open_clipboard.call(0) != 0)

      sleep 0.02
    end
    return false unless opened

    handle = nil
    transferred = false
    begin
      return false if empty_clipboard.call.zero?

      data = text.to_s.encode('UTF-16LE').b + "\x00\x00".b
      handle = global_alloc.call(0x0042, data.bytesize) # GMEM_MOVEABLE | GMEM_ZEROINIT
      return false if handle.to_i.zero?

      locked = global_lock.call(handle)
      return false if locked.to_i.zero?

      begin
        Fiddle::Pointer.new(locked.to_i)[0, data.bytesize] = data
      ensure
        global_unlock.call(handle)
      end
      transferred = !set_data.call(13, handle).to_i.zero? # CF_UNICODETEXT
    ensure
      global_free.call(handle) if handle && !transferred
      close_clipboard.call
    end
    transferred
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  def self.copy_to_clipboard(text)
    return true if copy_to_windows_clipboard(text)

    cmd = if RUBY_PLATFORM =~ /mingw|mswin|cygwin/ then 'clip'
          elsif RUBY_PLATFORM =~ /darwin/ then 'pbcopy'
          else 'xclip -selection clipboard'
          end
    IO.popen(cmd, 'w') { |io| io.write(text.to_s) }
    $?.nil? || $?.success?
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  # *cal goto u3209357 (game room UID) or *cal goto 1234 (Lich room ID).
  def self.goto_room(ref)
    uid = ref.start_with?('u')
    num = ref.delete('u').to_i
    label = uid ? "u#{num}" : num.to_s # u-prefixed like exitwindow, so it pastes straight into ;go2
    copied = copy_to_clipboard(label)
    ids = if uid
            (Map.ids_from_uid(num) rescue []) || []
          else
            (Room[num] rescue nil) ? [num] : []
          end
    copy_note = copied ? "Room #{label} has been copied to your clipboard" : "Room #{label} could not be copied to your clipboard"
    if ids.empty?
      respond "Calendar: #{copy_note}, but it is not in your map database, so go2 cannot travel there."
    elsif running?('go2')
      respond "Calendar: #{copy_note}. go2 is already running, so stop it first if you want to travel there."
    else
      respond "Calendar: #{copy_note}. Starting go2 to travel there."
      start_script('go2', [uid ? "u#{num}" : num.to_s])
    end
  end

  # ---------- combined / grouped ----------

  # Combined (default): every calendar mixed into one list.
  # Grouped: one section per calendar, in the order of the checkboxes.
  def self.grouped?
    CharSettings['grouped'] == true
  end

  def self.set_grouped(value)
    CharSettings['grouped'] = value
    respond(value ? 'Calendar: Events are now grouped by calendar.' : 'Calendar: All calendars are now combined into one list.')
    render
  end

  # One section per day.
  def self.days_lines(occs)
    lines = []
    occs.group_by { |o| local(o.start).to_date }.each do |date, list|
      lines << day_header(date)
      list.each { |o| lines << event_line(o) }
      lines << ''
    end
    lines
  end

  # One bold section per enabled calendar that has events; the block turns that
  # calendar's events into lines. Calendars with nothing are named at the end.
  def self.grouped_lines(occs, nothing_from)
    lines = []
    quiet = []
    @visible_sections = []
    order.map { |k| CALENDARS.find { |c| c[:key] == k } }.each do |cal|
      next unless enabled.include?(cal[:key])

      list = occs.select { |o| o.event.cal == cal[:key] }
      if list.empty?
        quiet << cal[:name]
        next
      end
      arrow = @visible_sections.empty? ? '' : "  <d cmd='*cal up #{cal[:key]}'>#{UP_ARROW}</d>"
      @visible_sections << cal[:key]
      lines << "<pushBold/>#{xml(cal[:name])}<popBold/>#{arrow}"
      lines.concat(yield(list))
    end
    lines << "Nothing #{nothing_from} from #{sentence_list(quiet)}." unless quiet.empty?
    lines
  end

  # ---------- views ----------

  def self.render
    @shown = []
    case @view
    when :week then render_week
    when :month then render_month
    when :day then render_day
    when :event then render_event
    else render_upcoming
    end
  end

  def self.render_upcoming
    lines = header(false)
    now = Time.now
    occs = CalendarEngine.occurrences(events, now, now + UPCOMING_DAYS * 86_400).first(UPCOMING_MAX)
    lines << (@events.empty? ? 'Downloading calendars, this takes a few seconds the first time...' : "Nothing scheduled in the next #{UPCOMING_DAYS} days.") if occs.empty?
    if grouped? && !occs.empty?
      all = CalendarEngine.occurrences(events, now, now + UPCOMING_DAYS * 86_400)
      lines.concat(grouped_lines(all, "in the next #{UPCOMING_DAYS} days") { |list| days_lines(list.first(UPCOMING_MAX)) })
    else
      lines.concat(days_lines(occs))
    end
    write(lines)
  end

  def self.week_start(date)
    date - date.wday
  end

  def self.render_week
    lines = header(true)
    first = week_start(@anchor)
    lines << "<pushBold/>Week of #{first.strftime('%b %-d')} - #{(first + 6).strftime('%b %-d, %Y')}<popBold/>"
    lines << ''
    from, = day_bounds(first)
    to, = day_bounds(first + 7)
    occs = CalendarEngine.occurrences(events, from, to)
    if grouped?
      lines.concat(grouped_lines(occs, 'this week') { |list| days_lines(list) })
      return write(lines)
    end
    7.times do |i|
      date = first + i
      ds, de = day_bounds(date)
      list = occs.select { |o| o.start >= ds && o.start < de }
      lines << day_header(date)
      list.empty? ? lines << '    (nothing scheduled)' : list.each { |o| lines << event_line(o) }
      lines << ''
    end
    write(lines)
  end

  def self.render_month
    lines = header(true)
    first = Date.new(@anchor.year, @anchor.month, 1)
    last = Date.new(@anchor.year, @anchor.month, -1)
    from, = day_bounds(first)
    to, = day_bounds(last + 1)
    counts = Hash.new(0)
    CalendarEngine.occurrences(events, from, to).each { |o| counts[local(o.start).to_date] += 1 }

    lines << "<pushBold/>#{first.strftime('%B %Y')}<popBold/>"
    lines << '<output class="mono"/>'
    lines << %w[Su Mo Tu We Th Fr Sa].map { |d| d.ljust(MONTH_CELL) }.join.rstrip
    row = ' ' * (MONTH_CELL * first.wday)
    (first..last).each do |date|
      count = counts[date]
      cell = date == Date.today ? "[#{date.day}]" : date.day.to_s
      cell += "(#{count})" if count > 0
      row += dlink("*cal day #{date.iso8601}", cell) + (' ' * [MONTH_CELL - cell.size, 1].max)
      if date.wday == 6 || date == last
        lines << row.rstrip
        row = ''
      end
    end
    lines << '<output class=""/>'
    lines << '(n) = number of events. Click a day to see them.'
    write(lines)
  end

  def self.render_day
    lines = header(true)
    lines << "<pushBold/>#{@anchor.strftime('%A, %B %-d, %Y')}<popBold/>"
    lines << dlink('*cal back', '[back]') unless @stack.empty?
    lines << ''
    from, to = day_bounds(@anchor)
    occs = CalendarEngine.occurrences(events, from, to).select { |o| o.start >= from }
    lines << '  (nothing scheduled)' if occs.empty?
    if grouped? && !occs.empty?
      lines.concat(grouped_lines(occs, 'on this day') { |list| list.map { |o| event_line(o) } + [''] })
    else
      occs.each { |o| lines << event_line(o) }
    end
    write(lines)
  end

  def self.render_event
    occ = @detail
    ev = occ.event
    cal = CALENDARS.find { |c| c[:key] == ev.cal }
    lines = ['<pushBold/>GemStone IV Calendar<popBold/>', dlink('*cal back', '[back]'), '']
    lines << "<pushBold/>#{xml(title(ev))}<popBold/>"
    s = local(occ.start)
    if occ.all_day
      days = ((occ.finish - occ.start) / 86_400.0).round
      lines << (days > 1 ? "#{s.strftime('%a %b %-d')} - #{(s.to_date + days - 1).strftime('%a %b %-d, %Y')} (all day)" : "#{s.strftime('%a %b %-d, %Y')} (all day)")
    else
      lines << "#{s.strftime('%a %b %-d, %Y  %l:%M %p').squeeze(' ')} - #{local(occ.finish).strftime('%l:%M %p').strip} #{zone_abbr(s)}"
    end
    lines << "Where: #{link_rooms(xml(ev.location))}" unless ev.location.empty?
    lines << "Calendar: #{cal ? cal[:name] : ev.cal}#{ev.rrule ? '  (repeats)' : ''}"
    if alarmable?(occ)
      @shown << occ
      idx = @shown.size - 1
      lines << if alarm?(occ)
                 "Alarm: #{ALARM_ICON} on  <d cmd='*cal alarm #{idx}'>[turn off]</d>"
               else
                 "Alarm: off  <d cmd='*cal alarm #{idx}'>[+ set alarm]</d>"
               end
    end
    lines << ''
    CalendarEngine.plain_text(ev.description).split("\n").each { |l| lines << link_rooms(xml(l)) }
    write(lines)
  end

  # ---------- alarms ----------

  ALARM_MINUTES = [60, 45, 30, 15, 5].freeze # warnings before an alarmed event starts
  ALARM_ICON = '&#x23F0;'.freeze             # alarm clock, as an entity so this file stays ASCII

  def self.alarm_key(occ)
    "#{occ.event.uid}|#{occ.start.to_i}"
  end

  # A plain Ruby copy of a value read from CharSettings. Some Lich versions hand
  # back settings proxies (and views of them from map/select/each); writing into
  # one of those, e.g. a['fired'] = ..., makes Lich try to save it and fail with
  # "this element of a view ... is not found in the settings". Built with each
  # so no proxy survives, whatever version of Lich is running.
  def self.plain(obj)
    if obj.is_a?(Hash)
      copy = {}
      obj.each { |k, v| copy[plain(k)] = plain(v) }
      copy
    elsif obj.is_a?(Array)
      copy = []
      obj.each { |v| copy << plain(v) }
      copy
    elsif obj.is_a?(String) then String.new(obj.to_str)
    elsif obj.is_a?(Integer) then obj.to_int
    elsif obj.is_a?(Float) then obj.to_f
    else obj
    end
  end

  def self.alarms
    list = plain(CharSettings['alarms'])
    return [] unless list.is_a?(Array)

    list.select { |a| a.is_a?(Hash) && a['start'] }.each do |a|
      a['start'] = a['start'].to_i
      a['fired'] = a['fired'].is_a?(Array) ? a['fired'] : []
    end
  end

  def self.save_alarms(list)
    CharSettings['alarms'] = list
  end

  def self.alarm?(occ)
    key = alarm_key(occ)
    alarms.any? { |a| a['key'] == key }
  end

  def self.alarmable?(occ)
    !occ.all_day && occ.start > Time.now
  end

  # Clickable marker left of the start time: "+" to set an alarm, the alarm clock to clear it.
  def self.alarm_marker(occ, index)
    return ' ' unless alarmable?(occ)

    label = alarm?(occ) ? ALARM_ICON : '+'
    "<d cmd='*cal alarm #{index}'>#{label}</d>"
  end

  def self.toggle_alarm(index)
    occ = @shown[index.to_i]
    return respond('Calendar: That event is no longer on screen. Please select it again.') unless occ
    return respond('Calendar: Alarms can only be set for timed events that have not started yet.') unless alarmable?(occ)

    list = alarms
    key = alarm_key(occ)
    name = CalendarEngine.to_ascii(title(occ.event))
    if list.any? { |a| a['key'] == key }
      list.reject! { |a| a['key'] == key }
      respond "Calendar: Your alarm for #{name} has been turned off."
    else
      list << { 'key' => key, 'title' => name, 'start' => occ.start.to_i, 'fired' => [] }
      respond "Calendar: An alarm has been set for #{name} at #{local(occ.start).strftime('%-I:%M %p')}. " \
              'You will be warned 1 hour, 45 minutes, 30 minutes, 15 minutes and 5 minutes before it starts.'
    end
    save_alarms(list)
    render
  end

  # "Fri Nov 13, 8:00 PM" -- single spaces, no padded hour.
  def self.alarm_when(alarm)
    Time.at(alarm['start']).strftime('%a %b %-d, %-I:%M %p')
  end

  def self.list_alarms
    list = alarms.sort_by { |a| a['start'] }
    return respond('Calendar: You have no alarms set.') if list.empty?

    respond((["Calendar: You have #{list.size} alarm#{list.size == 1 ? '' : 's'} set:"] + list.map { |a| "  #{alarm_when(a)} - #{a['title']}" }).join("
"))
  end

  def self.minutes_text(mins)
    mins >= 58 ? '1 hour' : "#{mins} minute#{mins == 1 ? '' : 's'}"
  end

  LOGIN_SUMMARY_DELAY = 60 # seconds after the script starts

  def self.time_until(seconds)
    mins = (seconds / 60.0).round
    return "in #{mins} min" if mins < 60

    hours = (mins / 60.0).round
    return "in #{hours} hour#{hours == 1 ? '' : 's'}" if hours < 48

    "in #{(hours / 24.0).round} days"
  end

  # Echoed once, about a minute after the script starts (i.e. after login):
  # every event with an alarm set, soonest first. Says nothing if none are set.
  def self.alarm_summary!
    now = Time.now.to_i
    list = alarms.select { |a| a['start'] > now }.sort_by { |a| a['start'] }
    return if list.empty?

    # One echo, so it shows as a single [calendar_sagapanel: ...] block.
    lines = ["You have #{list.size} event alarm#{list.size == 1 ? '' : 's'} set:"]
    list.each { |a| lines << "  #{alarm_when(a)} - #{a['title']} (#{time_until(a['start'] - now)})" }
    echo lines.join("
")
  end

  def self.alarm_message(title, mins, start)
    "CALENDAR ALARM: #{title} starts in #{minutes_text(mins)} " \
      "(#{Time.at(start).strftime('%-I:%M %p')})."
  end

  # *cal alarmtest: echoes one warning, exactly as a real alarm would, for a
  # random upcoming event and a random warning time. Nothing is saved, so it is
  # safe for trying out highlights and sounds.
  def self.alarm_test
    now = Time.now
    picks = CalendarEngine.occurrences(events, now, now + 30 * 86_400).select { |o| alarmable?(o) }
    return respond('Calendar: There are no upcoming timed events to test an alarm with.') if picks.empty?

    occ = picks.sample
    echo alarm_message(CalendarEngine.to_ascii(title(occ.event)), ALARM_MINUTES.sample, occ.start.to_i)
  end

  # Called from the main loop. Echoes each warning once; if Lich was not
  # running when several warnings came due, only the latest one is echoed.
  def self.check_alarms!
    now = Time.now.to_i
    list = alarms
    return if list.empty?

    changed = false
    list.each do |a|
      mins = (a['start'] - now) / 60.0
      due = ALARM_MINUTES.select { |m| mins <= m && !a['fired'].include?(m) }
      next if due.empty?

      a['fired'] = a['fired'] + due
      changed = true
      next if mins <= 0

      echo alarm_message(a['title'], mins.round, a['start'])
    end
    started = list.select { |a| a['start'] <= now }
    list -= started
    save_alarms(list) if changed || !started.empty?
    render unless started.empty?
  end

  # ---------- navigation ----------

  def self.show_view(view)
    @view = view
    @stack = []
    @anchor = Date.today
    render
  end

  def self.step(direction)
    case @view
    when :week then @anchor += 7 * direction
    when :month then @anchor = @anchor >> direction
    when :day then @anchor += direction
    else return
    end
    render
  end

  def self.today!
    @anchor = Date.today
    render
  end

  def self.push_view
    @stack << [@view, @anchor, @detail]
    @stack.shift while @stack.size > 10
  end

  def self.show_day(str)
    date = Date.iso8601(str) rescue nil
    return respond('Calendar: Please enter the date as *cal day YYYY-MM-DD, for example *cal day 2026-11-14.') unless date

    push_view unless @view == :day
    @view = :day
    @anchor = date
    render
  end

  def self.show_event(index)
    occ = @shown[index.to_i]
    return respond('Calendar: That event is no longer on screen. Please select it again.') unless occ

    push_view
    @detail = occ
    @view = :event
    render
  end

  def self.back!
    if @stack.empty?
      @view = :upcoming
      @anchor = Date.today
    else
      @view, @anchor, @detail = @stack.pop
    end
    render
  end

  HELP = [
    '*cal / *cal upcoming   - Upcoming view',
    '*cal alarm <n>         - set/clear an alarm (click the + or alarm clock)',
    '*cal alarms            - list alarms',
    '*cal alarmtest         - echo a sample alarm for a random event',
    '*cal back              - back from an event or day',
    '*cal combine           - mix all calendars into one list (default)',
    '*cal day YYYY-MM-DD    - one day',
    '*cal goto <room>       - copy a room number and go2 there (click it in event details)',
    '*cal group             - separate the list into a section per calendar',
    '*cal month             - Month view',
    '*cal next / *cal prev  - move forward/back',
    '*cal refresh           - re-download calendars',
    '*cal show <calendar>   - toggle prime, premium, platinum, general, houses, mho, towncrier',
    '*cal today             - jump to today',
    '*cal up <calendar>     - move a calendar up in the grouped list (the up arrow)',
    '*cal week              - Week view'
  ].freeze

  def self.handle(arg)
    case arg
    when '', /\Aupcoming\z/i then show_view(:upcoming)
    when /\Aweek\z/i then show_view(:week)
    when /\Amonth\z/i then show_view(:month)
    when /\Aday\s+(\S+)\z/i then show_day(Regexp.last_match(1))
    when /\Aevent\s+(\d+)\z/i then show_event(Regexp.last_match(1))
    when /\Aback\z/i then back!
    when /\Acombine\z/i then set_grouped(false)
    when /\Agroup\z/i then set_grouped(true)
    when /\Agoto\s+(u?\d+)\z/i then goto_room(Regexp.last_match(1).downcase)
    when /\Aup\s+(\S+)\z/i then move_up(Regexp.last_match(1))
    when /\Anext\z/i then step(1)
    when /\Aprev\z/i then step(-1)
    when /\Atoday\z/i then today!
    when /\Ashow\s+(\S+)\z/i then toggle_calendar(Regexp.last_match(1))
    when /\Arefresh\z/i then start_refresh!(announce: true)
    when /\Aalarm\s+(\d+)\z/i then toggle_alarm(Regexp.last_match(1))
    when /\Aalarms\z/i then list_alarms
    when /\Aalarm\s*test\z/i then alarm_test
    when /\Ahelp\z/i then HELP.each { |l| respond l }
    else respond("Calendar: '#{arg}' is not a calendar command. Type *cal help to see the list of commands.")
    end
  end
end

hook_id = "#{Script.current.name}_upstream"
UpstreamHook.remove(hook_id) rescue nil
UpstreamHook.add(hook_id, proc do |command|
  if command.strip =~ /\A(?:<c>)?\*cal(?:endar)?(?:\s+(.*))?\z/i
    CalendarPanel.queue << Regexp.last_match(1).to_s.strip
    nil
  else
    command
  end
end)

_respond("<streamWindow id='#{CalendarPanel::WINDOW_ID}' title='Calendar' ifClosed='' resident='true'/>")
sleep 0.05
_respond("<exposeStream id='#{CalendarPanel::WINDOW_ID}'/>")

before_dying do
  UpstreamHook.remove(hook_id) rescue nil
  _respond("<closeStream id='#{CalendarPanel::WINDOW_ID}'/>")
end

CalendarPanel.load_cached!
CalendarPanel.render
CalendarPanel.start_refresh! if CalendarPanel.stale?
echo 'The calendar panel is now active. Type *cal help to see the list of commands.'

last_minute = Time.now.min
login_summary_at = Time.now + CalendarPanel::LOGIN_SUMMARY_DELAY
loop do
  begin
    arg = CalendarPanel.queue.pop(true) rescue nil
    if arg
      CalendarPanel.handle(arg)
    else
      CalendarPanel.start_refresh! if CalendarPanel.stale?
      CalendarPanel.poll_refresh!
      CalendarPanel.check_alarms!
      if login_summary_at && Time.now >= login_summary_at
        login_summary_at = nil
        CalendarPanel.alarm_summary!
      end
      # Keep the Upcoming list current (drops finished events) every 15 minutes.
      if Time.now.min != last_minute && (Time.now.min % 15).zero?
        CalendarPanel.render if CalendarPanel.instance_variable_get(:@view) == :upcoming
      end
      last_minute = Time.now.min
      sleep 0.5
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "Calendar: An error occurred in the calendar panel (#{e.message})."
    sleep 1
  end
end
